message.content:
Plastic cable ties are generally classified in HTSUS 3926.90 (other articles of plastics), and the specific statistical suffix is usually 3926.90.9990 ("Other"). Alternatively, 3926.90.99 is the basic "Other" provision under 3926.90.

CBP rulings on nylon cable ties for general use generally place them in 3926.90.9990, though some older rulings used 3926.90.9880 or 3926.90.9985. Cable ties used with electrical wiring could also be classified in 3925 or 8547, but 8547 covers insulating fittings and applies only to ties that are designed for electrical insulation purposes, so it does not fit here. I'll go with 3926.90.9990.

{"hts_code": "3926.90.9990", "reason": "A standard plastic (nylon) zip/cable tie is an article of plastics not elsewhere specified, classified in heading 3926 as other articles of plastics under subheading 3926.90.9990."}
